{"toolCallId":"call_6ac9fcf63b2d4145813fc7f3ada9d2f3","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"total 80\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel   449 26 Oct 18:10:58 2026 description.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  5563 26 Oct 18:14:14 2026 graph-metadata.json\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  2488 26 Oct 18:13:21 2026 implementation-summary.md\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  5913 26 Oct 18:13:00 2026 plan.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  wheel    96 26 Oct 18:10:58 2026 scratch\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  8211 26 Oct 18:14:00 2026 spec.md\n-rw-------@ 1 michelkerkmeester  wheel  3113 26 Oct 18:14:01 2026 tasks.md\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-004 | A missing, empty, non-integer, negative or greater-than-100 argument is rejected with exit `1` and a message on stderr. A malformed argument never produces exit `3`, because `3` must keep meaning \"completion below the floor\". | `--min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -5` and `--min-percent 101` each exit `1` and print an error; no report is emitted. |\n| REQ-005 | In `--file` mode, where the report has no \"Overall Completion\" line, the gate compares the completion figure that mode does report. | On a single file at 40%: `--file <path> --min-percent 50` exits `3`; `--file <path> --min-percent 40` exits `0`. |\n| REQ-006 | `--help` lists the option, and the exit-code comment block at the end of the script names status `3`. | `--help` output contains `--min-percent`; the trailing comment block documents `0`, `1` and `3`. |\n| REQ-007 | When `--json` and `--min-percent` are passed together, the JSON report gains a boolean field `min_percent_met`: `true` when the Overall Completion figure is at or above `N`, `false` when it is below. | On a fixture packet whose reported completion is 75%: `--json --min-percent 80` emits `\"min_percent_met\": false`; `--json --min-percent 75` and `--json --min-percent 70` emit `\"min_percent_met\": true`. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n- [ ] T003 Declare the threshold global as empty in the globals block, so an unset value means \"no gate\" (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--min-percent` case arm before the `*` fallback, with the argument-count guard and the integer 0-100 validation that exits `1` on a bad value (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T005 Add the post-output gate: compare the figure the active mode reports against the threshold and exit `3` below it, `0` at or above it (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T006 Document the option in `show_help` and extend the trailing exit-code comment block to cover `0`, `1` and `3` (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n- [ ] T010 Emit the `min_percent_met` boolean in the `--json` report when a threshold is set, true at or above it and false below (REQ-007) (`calculate-completeness.sh`)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wa3f8a76d29/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"1754d0","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
